# Walks the service menu down to the sequential lamp test and holds there long
# enough to capture the full LC1..LC64 single-lamp walk (F18).
#
# Navigation (F14): TEST/KEYCODE_7 opens and exits the menu, the left flipper
# (KEYCODE_LSHIFT) scrolls, the right flipper (KEYCODE_RSHIFT) selects, START
# goes back.  The path is TEST -> record 0 (root) -> record 3 (TECNICO, the
# root's 3rd item, cursor 2) -> record 22 (TEST TABLERO, TECNICO's 1st item,
# cursor 0, no scroll needed) -> record 25 (LUCES, TEST TABLERO's 2nd item,
# cursor 1) -> record 35 (TEST LUCES 1, LUCES' 1st item, cursor 0, no scroll).
# The record numbers are the ones already established in F14's menu tree. A
# fresh boot with no DIP override renders them in English (TECHNICAL / BOARD
# TEST / LIGHTS / "- LIGHT TEST -") rather than the manual's Spanish TECNICO /
# TEST TABLERO / LUCES, since country 5 (Spain) is not the default (F11);
# F14 shows the root's own items render identically placed in both languages,
# so the same is expected, not separately verified here, for these records.
#
# An early START (frame 40) clears iomoon's first-run NVRAM "PRESS START"
# seed screen -- without it no later key reaches the menu.
  40 tap 8 KEYCODE_1
  60 mark boot
 400 mark attract
 600 tap 8 KEYCODE_7
 700 mark menu-root
 800 tap 8 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
 900 tap 8 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
1000 mark menu-root-cursor-technical
1100 tap 8 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
1200 mark menu-technical
1300 tap 8 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
1400 mark menu-board-test
1500 tap 8 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
1600 mark menu-board-test-cursor-lights
1700 tap 8 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
1800 mark menu-lights
1900 tap 8 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
2000 mark lamp-test-1-running
6500 quit
